<title>TURKEY: Chevron to sign accord to develop Tengiz oilfield.</title>
<headline>Chevron to sign accord to develop Tengiz oilfield.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chevron Corp will sign a $250-million acccord with Bechtel and Turkey's ENKA to increase crude output at Kazakhstan's greater Tengiz oilfields, an ENKA official said.</p>
<p>The official said the deal would be signed in Istanbul on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The accord aims to increase the oil output capacity at the greater Tengiz oilfields by 30 percent within two years to 11 million tonnes in 1999,&quot; the official, who declined to be named, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said about $100 million of the total investment would be made this year and $150 million in 1998.</p>
</text>
